<article class="env-remark" id="04C5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04C5">Remark <span data-tag="04C5">59.48.7</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/04C4" data-tag="04C4">59.48.6</a> the case $\tau = fppf$ is missing. The reason is that given a ring $A$, an ideal $I$ and a faithfully flat, finitely presented ring map $A/I \to \overline{B}$, there is no reason to think that one can find <em>any</em> flat finitely presented ring map $A \to B$ with $B/IB \not= 0$ such that $A/I \to B/IB$ factors through $\overline{B}$. Hence the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/04C3" data-tag="04C3">59.48.5</a> does not work for the fppf topology. In fact it is likely false that $f_{big, *} : \textit{Ab}((\mathit{Sch}/X)_{fppf}) \to \textit{Ab}((\mathit{Sch}/Y)_{fppf})$ is exact when $f$ is a closed immersion. If you know an example, please email <a href="mailto:stacks.project@gmail.com">stacks.project@gmail.com</a>. </p>
</article>